      "rationale": "All four tests target the same root-cause bug: FilterStack.__init__ has `if not (strip_semicolon):` instead of `if strip_semicolon:` when deciding to register StripTrailingSemicolonFilter, so by default (strip_semicolon=False, used by both sqlparse.format and sqlparse.split) trailing semicolons are silently stripped, while explicitly passing strip_semicolon=True leaves them untouched - the exact opposite of the documented contract (\"If True, remove trailing semicolons (default: False)\" in sqlparse.split's docstring, and format() never stripping semicolons at all). Since virtually every SQL snippet in the real test suite ends with a semicolon, this single inverted condition explains the breadth of the reported regression ('stdout' CLI output, 'format: notransform of quoted crlf', 'format reindent: stmts', and dozens more), and the expected strings are derived directly from the library's own documented default and from tracing the (otherwise correct) StripWhitespaceFilter/ReindentFilter/SerializerUnicode logic by hand.",
